  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Goalkeeper to goalkeeper",
  "description": "Two equal teams, for example 4v4, on an area of about 25 × 15 metres split into three zones with cones. A goalkeeper stands on each short side (J) and always plays with the team that has the ball.\n\nThe team with the ball must play from one goalkeeper to the other. On the way, a player has to control the ball in every zone before it may be played to the goalkeeper. If they manage it they score a point, and the receiving goalkeeper starts the other way. If the other team wins the ball, the same applies to them.\n\nPlay two minutes at a time with a minute of mobility in between. Harder: a point only counts if the opponents never touched the ball, and when the goalkeeper starts the defenders must be behind a line (for example halfway) before they may press. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Make yourselves available in every zone – one wide and one deep."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Receive with your body open so you can turn forwards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: talk, and play to the player who is facing forwards or half-turned."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defenders: step into the pass as your opponent receives, and work together to close the lanes."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
